.TH SLIDELITE 1 "October 2026" "SlideLite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slidelite \- lightweight PowerPoint presentation viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slidelite
[\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR | \fB\-\-presentation\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slidelite
opens PowerPoint (.pptx, .ppsx, .pptm) presentations for viewing and presenting.
It never modifies the presentation, never runs macros and never uses the network.
Without a file it shows the welcome screen with recent presentations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Open the viewer window fullscreen.
.TP
.B \-\-presentation
Start the slide show immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage information.
.SH KEYS
In the slide show: Right/Down/Space/Page Down next, Left/Up/Page Up previous,
Home/End first/last slide, number then Enter go to slide, B/W black/white screen,
Esc end the show.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/slidelite/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/slidelite/recent.json
Recently opened presentations (local only).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/ammarqaisar11a55/SlideLite-Lightweight-PPTX-Viewer-for-Ubuntu
